== RDF / OWL standards state ==

As of 2026, RDF 1.2 Concepts and RDF 1.2 Semantics are W3C Candidate Recommendation Snapshots. Stable Core prose should explain version-independent RDF; a dated standards section may describe RDF 1.2 additions such as triple terms and directional language-tagged strings.

OWL 2 remains the W3C Recommendation family used for formal ontology representation. Its direct semantics is closely related to SROIQ description logic.

== Source roles ==

* SEP: semantics, ontology, identity, concepts, categories and philosophical distinctions.
* Gruber; Studer/Benjamins/Fensel: applied ontology and knowledge engineering.
* Davis/Shrobe/Szolovits; Brachman/Levesque; Description Logic Handbook: KR and reasoning.
* Quillian and later semantic-memory work: semantic-network history.
* Hogan et al.: knowledge graph synthesis.
* W3C: RDF, RDFS, OWL, SKOS and Semantic Web formal specifications.
* ISO/IEC 21838: top-level ontology requirements/examples.
* ISO 25964: thesauri / knowledge organization.
* NISO / DCMI: metadata.
* Wikipedia/Scholarpedia: orientation/discovery only where stronger sources exist.

